# Contract Proof

Command:

```text
cmd /c npm run test --workspace @ocentra-parent/activity-domain -- activity-surface
```

Result:

```text
PASS packages/activity-domain/tests/activity-surface.test.ts
Tests: 17 passed
```

Coverage:

- App-use read-model rows now decode typed app/game projection fields:
  `productKind`, `classificationState`, `inventoryState`, `runtimeState`,
  `foregroundState`, `capabilityStatus`, `lastObservedAt`,
  `inventoryRowCount`, `runningRowCount`, `foregroundRowCount`, and
  `dailyRollupCount`.
- Games read-model rows now decode the same state spine plus
  `launcherRowCount`.
- Contract tests prove inventory, running, and foreground states remain
  separate on app-use rows.
- Contract tests prove game launcher/session counts are separate from native
  app usage counts.

Command:

```text
cmd /c npm run build:contracts
cmd /c npm run test --workspace @ocentra-parent/agent-protocol-domain -- activity-surface-adapter
```

Result:

```text
PASS packages/agent-protocol-domain/tests/activity-surface-adapter.test.ts
Tests: 15 passed
```

Coverage:

- Activity surface read-model events parse typed app-use rows with source row
  counts.
- The adapter parser keeps service event payloads in the shared contract layer.
- The first adapter run required `build:contracts`; after generated package
  output was refreshed, the focused adapter test passed.

No-claim boundaries represented in the contract row fields:

- Inventory state is distinct from runtime state.
- Runtime state is distinct from foreground state.
- Foreground state does not contain content/title knowledge.
- Launcher row count is separate from proved game session count.
- Capability status can remain `notClaimed`, `permissionLimited`, `stale`,
  `unsupportedPlatform`, `unavailable`, or `adapterError`.
